{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1863","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I. Redundant Routes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a tree with $$$n$$$ vertices labeled $$$1, 2, \\ldots, n$$$. The length of a simple path in the tree is the number of vertices in it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are to select a set of simple paths of length at least $$$2$$$ each, but you cannot simultaneously select two distinct paths contained one in another. Find the largest possible size of such a set."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, a set $$$S$$$ of vertices is called a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"route"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it contains "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at least two vertices"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and coincides with the set of vertices of a simple path in the tree. A collection of distinct routes is called a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"timetable"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". A route $$$S$$$ in a timetable $$$T$$$ is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"redundant"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there is a different route $$$S' \\in T$$$ such that $$$S \\subset S'$$$. A timetable is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"efficient"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it contains no redundant routes. Find the largest possible number of routes in an efficient timetable."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 3000$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The $$$i$$$-th of the following $$$n - 1$$$ lines contains two integers $$$u_i$$$ and $$$v_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le n$$$, $$$u_i \\neq v_i$$$) — the numbers of vertices connected by the $$$i$$$-th edge."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the given edges form a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the answer to the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n2 1\n3 2\n4 3\n5 3\n6 4\n7 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, possible efficient timetables are $$$\\{\\{1, 2\\}, \\{1, 3\\}, \\{1, 4\\}\\}$$$ and $$$\\{\\{1, 2, 3\\}, \\{1, 2, 4\\}, \\{1, 3, 4\\}\\}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, we can choose $$$\\{ \\{1, 2, 3\\}, \\{2, 3, 4\\}, \\{3, 4, 6\\}, \\{2, 3, 5\\}, \\{3, 4, 5\\}, \\{3, 4, 7\\}, \\{4, 6, 7\\}\\}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"I","problemCode":"1863I","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1863/problem/I"}